Create weekly power rankings for a fantasy baseball league based on the scheduled matchups
for each scoring period.
please use the fantrax api collection that was previously created
and the GO auth client that is already in place

I would like a JSON object returned
1. For every scoring period I would like the following data returned:
  scoringPeriod,
  date,
  teamId,
  teamName,
  logoUrl,
  periodPoints,
  periodWin,
  periodWinsVsAll,
  totalPoints,
  totalWins,
  totalWinsVsAll,
  pointsPowerRank,
  winsPowerRank,
  winsVsAllPowerRank,
  totalPowerRank,
  change

2. Definitions
periodPoints: total points scored by an individual team during a scoring period. If a
        team has more than one matchup in a scoring period please do not total the points.
        The score should only be counted once.
periodWin: whichever team in the matchup that has the highest score wins the matchup. If a
team has multiple matchups in the same scoring period they will accumulate all wins for
that period. For example, if a team has two matchups in a scoring period and they win
both matchups then their periodWin total will equal 2
periodWinsVsAll: for each scoring period please compare all teams' total scores against
one another. A team will accumulate wins for every other team they have a higher score than
in that period. For example a team has a higher score than 8 other teams, in this instance their
total for periodWinsVsAll would be 8. The lowest scoring team will have 0.
totalPoints: this should be a total of all period points accumulated from every previous
scoring period and including the current scoring period
totalWins: this should be a total of all period wins accumulated from every previous
scoring period and including the current scoring period
totalWinsVsAll: this should be a total of all period winsVsAll accumulated from every previous
scoring period and including the current scoring period
pointsPowerRank: rank each team based on totalPoints. If scoringPeriod equals 1 then
rank the teams based on periodPoints. Base the rank on the number of teams in the league.
For this league there are 12 teams so the highest rank should be 12. The highest scoring team
will be ranked with 12 and the lowest scoring team will be ranked with 1. If an even number of teams are tied
in totalPoints then split the ranking for those teams and then skip a ranking for then next team.
For example two teams tie for the highest total points, their rank will each be 11.5 and the next
team would be ranked 10. If an odd number of teams has the same total then they will all have
the same rank and it will not be split.
winsPowerRank: use the same rules for pointsPowerRank but base the rankings on totalWins
winsVsAllPowerRank: same rules as pointsPowerRank but base the rankings on totalWinsVsAll
totalPowerRank = pointsPowerRank + winsPowerRank + winsVsAllPowerRank
change: difference between totalPowerRank from the previous period to the current period